# ── Python ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ── Regenerable stats (rebuilt by the pipeline) ──
data/stats.json
data/stats_history.jsonl

# NOTE: the ENRICHMENT caches (data/abstracts.json, data/abstracts_extra.json,
# data/crossref_cache.json, data/code_links.json, data/found_links.json) are
# TRACKED on purpose — same rationale as data/venue_links.json /
# data/incremental.json (notes below). When gitignored they were lost on every
# clean checkout / daily CI regenerate, so the published dataset silently dropped
# to ~12/1930 abstracts. Committing them keeps enrichment warm, cumulative and
# reproducible.

# ── Backups / temp / one-off artifacts (never meant to be tracked) ──
*.bak
data/incremental.json.bak
data/papers.json.pre_incremental
data/_surveys_tmp.json
data/_code_anthology.json
data/cvpr2026_hall.json
data/candidates_new.json
no_keyword_review.md

# NOTE: data/venue_links.json is TRACKED on purpose (same rationale as
# incremental.json). It is the enrichment cache mapping each paper to its
# resolved conference/journal venue, year and external link. When it was
# gitignored and lost, every clean checkout fell back to arXiv years and
# "arXiv"/"其他" venue names. Rebuilt from the committed papers.json
# (scripts/rebuild_venue_links.py) and kept current by update_pipeline.py so a
# fresh clone / CI checkout is never cold for venue resolution.

# NOTE: data/incremental.json is TRACKED on purpose. It is not a cache — it
# holds 827 harvested papers that exist in no other source file. While it was
# ignored, any clean checkout (i.e. every CI run) made generate.py rebuild
# papers.json from seed.json + manual_entries.yaml alone and silently shrink
# the dataset from 1897 to 1070. Keep it committed so generate.py is
# reproducible from a fresh clone.

# NOTE: docs/papers.json is a GENERATED duplicate of data/papers.json (needed
# by GitHub Pages). It is intentionally tracked. If you prefer a single source
# of truth, uncomment the next line and have CI run `generate.py` on deploy:
# docs/papers.json

# ── Internal assistant memory / local-only scratch (never publish) ──
.workbuddy/

# ── Generated social-preview background (intermediate, regenerable) ──
# The final social-preview.png (repo root) is the tracked artifact.
generated-images/
